---
import Patina from "../../components/Patina.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import { SOURCES_CHECKED, featureRows } from "../../data/compare";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";

const linkClass = "text-ink underline decoration-edge-strong underline-offset-4 transition hover:decoration-ink";
const verdicts = [
  {
    title: "Pick Mailpit",
    body: "if you want the widest feature set: HTML client compatibility scores, live link checks, SpamAssassin, POP3 and SMTP failure injection. It is mature and actively maintained.",
  },
  {
    title: "Pick RustMail",
    body: "if your tests live in CI: an assertion endpoint built for curl -f, a blocking rustmail assert command and an official GitHub Action, plus full-text search, auth results and a terminal UI.",
  },
  {
    title: "Move off MailHog",
    body: "it has had no release since 2020. Both alternatives listen on the same ports, so switching is a one-line change in your Docker Compose file.",
  },
];
---

<Layout
  title="RustMail vs Mailpit vs MailHog: local SMTP mail catchers compared"
  description="An honest comparison of three local SMTP mail catchers: features, CI support and maintenance, including where Mailpit is ahead of RustMail."
  path="/compare/"
>
  <Patina />

  <div class="relative z-10">
    <SiteNav />

    <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-12 pb-24 md:pt-20">
      <div class="max-w-3xl">
        <h1 class="font-brand text-4xl leading-[1.08] font-bold tracking-tight text-balance text-ink md:text-5xl">
          RustMail vs Mailpit vs MailHog
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
          Three local SMTP mail catchers with the same default ports. This page
          is written by the RustMail project, so it says where the others are
          stronger too.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-14 grid gap-x-10 gap-y-8 border-t border-edge pt-10 md:grid-cols-3">
        {
          verdicts.map((v) => (
            <div>
              <h2 class="font-brand text-xl font-bold text-ink">{v.title}</h2>
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-pretty text-ink-muted">{v.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>

      <section class="mt-20" aria-labelledby="features-title">
        <h2 id="features-title" class="font-brand text-3xl font-bold text-ink">Features</h2>
        <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-edge-strong">
          <table class="w-full min-w-[40rem] text-left text-sm">
            <thead class="bg-raised text-ink">
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" class="w-1/3 px-5 py-4 font-medium text-ink-muted">
                  <span class="sr-only">Feature</span>
                </th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold text-orange-400">RustMail</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">Mailpit</th>
                <th scope="col" class="px-5 py-4 font-semibold">MailHog</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-ink-muted">
              {
                featureRows.map((row) => (
                  <tr class="border-t border-edge">
                    <th scope="row" class="px-5 py-3.5 font-medium text-ink">{row.label}</th>
                    <td class="px-5 py-3.5 text-ink">{row.rustmail}</td>
                    <td class="px-5 py-3.5">{row.mailpit}</td>
                    <td class="px-5 py-3.5">{row.mailhog}</td>
                  </tr>
                ))
              }
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm text-ink-muted">
          "Not listed" means the feature is not in the project's README feature
          list as of {SOURCES_CHECKED}. Corrections are welcome as an issue on{" "}
          <a href="https://github.com/rustmailapp/rustmail-www/issues" class={linkClass}>GitHub</a>.
          For speed, memory and disk, see the{" "}
          <a href="https://docs.rustmail.app/benchmarks" class={linkClass}>benchmarks</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="mt-20 max-w-3xl">
        <h2 class="font-brand text-3xl font-bold text-ink">Switching from MailHog or Mailpit</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 text-ink-muted">
          Your app's SMTP settings do not change: RustMail listens on 1025 for
          SMTP and serves the inbox on 8025. Tests that call the MailHog or
          Mailpit HTTP API do need updating, because RustMail has its own{" "}
          <a href="https://docs.rustmail.app/api/" class={linkClass}>REST API</a>.
          For most CI checks the{" "}
          <a href="https://docs.rustmail.app/ci-integration/rest-assertions" class={linkClass}>assertion endpoint</a>{" "}
          replaces the polling code entirely.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2">
          <a href="https://docs.rustmail.app/getting-started/quick-start" class={linkClass}>Quick start</a>
          <a href="/guides/" class={linkClass}>Framework guides</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</Layout>
